From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: usbhid: add a quirk to send SET_IDLE on resume

The Huawei MCU 12d1:10b8 behind the keyboard, touchpad and pen pressure
marks every interface as suspended on SET_FEATURE(DEVICE_REMOTE_WAKEUP)
and holds that interface's IN reports until it sees SET_IDLE or an OUT
packet there. Both only count while the interface isn't already marked
active, and a SET_REPORT on any interface marks interface 0 active as a
side effect.

On resume interface 0 is bound to hid-generic and gets no request, then
mt_resume() on interface 2 sends SET_IDLE and SET_REPORT. Interface 2
works, interface 0 is left marked active but holding its reports, and
pen pressure stops until a bus reset. USB_QUIRK_RESET_RESUME fixes it
through hid_post_reset(), at the cost of the key press that woke the
system, which the MCU flushes on reset.

Send SET_IDLE in hid_resume() for devices with the new quirk. usbcore
resumes interfaces in descriptor order, which is ascending on this MCU,
so interface 0 sees it before interface 2 sends SET_REPORT. It goes
after hid_resume_common() because the reports queued in suspend leave
as soon as it arrives, about a millisecond apart and without waiting
for the previous one to go: with no IN URB pending, two of them can
share a packet, and hid_report_raw_event() only parses the first, which
loses a key release.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 include/linux/hid.h           |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c b/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c
index 96b0181cf..9b73158c7 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c
@@ -1659,6 +1659,20 @@ static int hid_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
 
 	status = hid_resume_common(hid, true);
 	dev_dbg(&intf->dev, "resume status %d\n", status);
+
+	/*
+	 * Not before hid_resume_common(): the device sends what it queued in
+	 * suspend as soon as it gets this, and reports that go out with no IN
+	 * pending can share a packet, of which hid_report_raw_event() parses
+	 * only the first.
+	 */
+	if (hid->quirks & HID_QUIRK_IDLE_ON_RESUME) {
+		status = hid_set_idle(interface_to_usbdev(intf),
+				      intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber, 0, 0);
+		if (status < 0)
+			hid_warn(hid, "SET_IDLE on resume failed: %d\n", status);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/include/linux/hid.h b/include/linux/hid.h
index 4e2422ec0..968fc2311 100644
--- a/include/linux/hid.h
+++ b/include/linux/hid.h
@@ -388,6 +388,7 @@ struct hid_item {
  * | @HID_QUIRK_INCREMENT_USAGE_ON_DUPLICATE:
  * | @HID_QUIRK_IGNORE_SPECIAL_DRIVER
  * | @HID_QUIRK_POWER_ON_AFTER_BACKLIGHT
+ * | @HID_QUIRK_IDLE_ON_RESUME: send SET_IDLE when the interface resumes
  * | @HID_QUIRK_FULLSPEED_INTERVAL:
  * | @HID_QUIRK_NO_INIT_REPORTS:
  * | @HID_QUIRK_NO_IGNORE:
@@ -416,6 +417,7 @@ struct hid_item {
 #define HID_QUIRK_NOINVERT			BIT(21)
 #define HID_QUIRK_IGNORE_SPECIAL_DRIVER		BIT(22)
 #define HID_QUIRK_POWER_ON_AFTER_BACKLIGHT	BIT(23)
+#define HID_QUIRK_IDLE_ON_RESUME		BIT(24)
 #define HID_QUIRK_FULLSPEED_INTERVAL		BIT(28)
 #define HID_QUIRK_NO_INIT_REPORTS		BIT(29)
 #define HID_QUIRK_NO_IGNORE			BIT(30)
